From e22d86cf16ceb7df1b58595b413abca17aa5ff84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Raul Moran <rmg@raulmoranguerra.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:31:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ClockSource: Find clock entries by handler with a
 dictionary

Every timer reload or read (ExchangeClockEntryWith, GetClockEntry) and
every Machine.ScheduleAction (AddClockEntry, then TryRemoveClockEntry
when the action runs) looks its entry up with a linear search comparing
delegates, allocating a closure each time. On a two-machine STM32H7
workload this search was 5.5% of all host samples (Misc.IndexOf and
Delegate.Equals under perf).

Keep a dictionary from each handler to the index of its first entry
beside the list, updated when entries are added, replaced or removed.
It finds what the linear search found: the same delegate equality and
the first entry for a handler. Entries without a handler are still
searched linearly.
